{"cells": [ {"cell_id":0,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":1,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":2,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":3,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":4,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":5,"family":"empty","group":"empty","source":"none","type":"empty"},  {"cell_id":6,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":7,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":8,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":9,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":10,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":11,"family":"empty","group":"empty","source":"none","type":"empty"},  {"cell_id":12,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":13,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":14,"family":"empty","group":"empty","source":"none","type":"empty"},  {"cell_id":15,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":16,"family":"untyped","group":"untyped","source":"none","type":"untyped"},  {"cell_id":17,"family":"empty","group":"empty","source":"none","type":"empty"} ],"counts": {"cells":18,"empty":4,"guided":0,"kept":0,"pending":14,"routed":14,"typed":0,"untyped":14},"guidelines_program_sha256":"5ea2aed2adcc1fcaaca6130be7f8eb16ee7f4484829ed7c612542ee4561e43bf","pmc_id":"PMC12597348","table_index":0,"table_uid":"PMC12597348/t0","type_program":"/Users/noname/Desktop/Type-Inference-Table-Parser/dataset-builder-agent/type_dsl_examples/sci_text.tdsl","type_raster": [ ["untyped", "untyped", "untyped" ],  ["untyped", "untyped", "empty" ],  ["untyped", "untyped", "untyped" ],  ["untyped", "untyped", "empty" ],  ["untyped", "untyped", "empty" ],  ["untyped", "untyped", "empty" ] ],"untyped_cells": [ {"cell_id":0,"text":"Criteria"},  {"cell_id":1,"text":"Inclusion"},  {"cell_id":2,"text":"Exclusion"},  {"cell_id":3,"text":"Population"},  {"cell_id":4,"text":"Hospitalised patients undergoing surgical procedures (where patients would normally be provided with anaesthesia by either an anaesthetist or a qualified anaesthetic practitioner) of any age group, and surgical specialty at any stage of the surgical pathway including preoperative, intraoperative, and postoperative periods."},  {"cell_id":6,"text":"Intervention"},  {"cell_id":7,"text":"Perioperative oxygen therapy, defined as oxygenation strategy where the primary purpose of the intervention is to optimise oxygenation/oxygen delivery, with the aim of preventing hypoxaemia or reducing complications during the perioperative period."},  {"cell_id":8,"text":"We excluded systematic reviews that primarily focus on intraoperative ventilation strategies (e.g. ventilatory rate, pressure and volume settings), hyperbaric oxygen therapy, and extracorporeal life support. 7 Reviews that examine preoxygenation strategies during tracheal intubation are excluded."},  {"cell_id":9,"text":"Comparator"},  {"cell_id":10,"text":"Any comparator or control."},  {"cell_id":12,"text":"Outcomes"},  {"cell_id":13,"text":"Primary outcomes: 1- Surgical site infection (SSI) within 30 days of follow-up after surgery: we followed definitions of the US Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (CDC) where possible. The CDC defines SSI as an infection related to a surgical procedure that occurs near the surgical site within 30 days after surgery (or up to 90 days after surgery where an implant is involved). 8 Reviews (and RCTs included in the reviews) that have adopted other definitions were included and examined if meeting other inclusion criteria, but differences in the outcome definitions were recorded and highlighted. 2- All-cause mortality within 30-days after surgery. Secondary outcomes: 1- Postoperative pulmonary complications (PPCs): defined according to the most recent consensus definition of PPC 9 as composite of respiratory diagnoses: (i) atelectasis detected on computed tomography or chest radiograph, (ii) pneumonia using US CDC criteria, (iii) acute respiratory distress syndrome (ARDS) using Berlin consensus definition, (iv) pulmonary aspiration (clear clinical history and radiological evidence). 2- Postoperative respiratory failure: including ARDS defined using Berlin consensus definition 10 and need for mechanical ventilation. Definitions for the above outcomes are recommended by the StEP-COMPAC Group. 9 We accepted similar outcomes defined differently in previous studies. Differences in the outcome definitions were recorded and highlighted. 3- Mortality up to the longest point of postoperative follow-up. 4- Length of hospital stay: the number of days from the day of surgery to hospital discharge or death. 5- ICU admission: unplanned admission to ICU within 14 days of surgery. 6- Quality of life. Further outcomes not listed above but are identified during the review and considered important by the Advisory Group were examined. Any post hoc addition of such outcomes is explicitly stated in our report."},  {"cell_id":15,"text":"Study design"},  {"cell_id":16,"text":"Systematic reviews and meta-analyses of RCTs that examine the use of perioperative oxygen therapy. We included systematic reviews that included both randomised and non-randomised studies if evidence summarised from RCTs was reported separately. Systematic reviews must have fulfilled a minimum of four methodological criteria as defined by Centre for Reviews and Dissemination, University of York, guidance to be included. 11 Specifically, reviews must have reported inclusion/exclusion criteria of studies, an adequate search strategy, synthesis of included studies, description of and quality assessment of included studies."} ]}
